# Line endings: this machine has core.autocrlf=true, which would check text out
# as CRLF. The extracted data (game/data, game/static) must stay byte-identical to
# what `npm run setup` writes, and bash scripts break on CRLF — so keep every
# text file LF in the working copy, on every checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch their bytes. Two of the three title .tilemap files
# contain no NUL byte, so git would otherwise guess they are text.
*.png     binary
*.tilemap binary
*.gbc     binary
*.gb      binary

# GitHub language stats — count TypeScript as JavaScript
*.ts  linguist-language=JavaScript
*.tsx linguist-language=JavaScript